  "lineage": "German-language sailor song as a commercial and choral genre, rooted in nineteenth-century Hamburg and Bremen harbour repertoire and in the 1930s-40s Hans Albers film songs (La Paloma, Auf der Reeperbahn nachts um halb eins), then dominated by Freddy Quinn's Polydor recordings from 1956 onward; typically moderate 3/4 or 4/4, orchestrated with strings, accordion and light rhythm section, sung in a warm baritone with a nostalgic Fernweh lyric and an anthemic male-chorus refrain, alongside an amateur Shanty-Chor branch singing the same material a cappella in four parts.",
